      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, so I'm prepping the methodology section for the Nature submission. To satisfy the reviewers regarding model-agnostic reproducibility, I need to show that the topological phase discovery isn't just an artifact of our specific fine-tuning. I'm planning to run a weight-pruning script to see if we can strip back the specialized heuristic layers and move to a more baseline architecture. Can you help me identify which latent layers or weight clusters are most \"expendable\" or least critical to the core physics engine so I can minimize the footprint?",
